%N A209585 Number of n X n 0..n arrays with every element equal to a diagonal or antidiagonal reflection.
%C A209585 a(n) has trailing zeros iff n is congruent to {7,9} modulo 10. - _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 04 2026
%H A209585 Stefano Spezia, <a href="/A209585/b209585.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..33</a>
%F A209585 a(n) = (n+1)^(2n-(n modulo 2))*((n+1)*(2n+1))^((n*n-2n+(n modulo 2))/4).
%e A209585 Some solutions for n=3:
%e A209585 ..0..0..1....3..0..2....2..0..1....0..3..0....2..0..0....3..3..3....0..2..2
%e A209585 ..0..1..1....1..0..0....0..1..3....2..3..3....2..3..0....2..1..3....2..1..2
%e A209585 ..3..1..2....0..1..1....1..3..3....3..2..2....2..2..3....0..2..0....0..2..3
%t A209585 a[n_]:=(n+1)^(2n-Mod[n,2])*((n+1)*(2n+1))^((n*n-2n+Mod[n,2])/4); Array[a,10] (* _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 04 2026 *)
